Why Is Maskless Lithography Becoming Important in Semiconductor Manufacturing?

Lithography is an essential stage in microfabrication because patterns transferred onto substrates determine the structures of semiconductor and other micro-scale devices. Traditional mask-based lithography can require mask preparation and modification when designs change.

Maskless lithography enables patterns to be generated directly onto photoresist without requiring a physical photomask. This approach can support flexible design changes and customized fabrication requirements.

The technology is particularly relevant to research laboratories, prototyping environments and specialized fabrication applications where multiple design iterations may be necessary.

